--
-- Tests for bc-interpretation-time.l4: when an enactment comes into force and from what moment it
-- binds (Interpretation Act (British Columbia), RSBC 1996, c. 238, ss 3, 4, 16(2), 26 and 29
-- "commencement" and "now").
--
-- Expected values were decided from the text before the first run:
--   * an Act or a portion for which no other date is provided commences on the date of assent
--     (s 3(2));
--   * an enactment commences "at the beginning of the day on which it comes into force" (s 4(1));
--   * "a reference to time in British Columbia is a reference to Pacific Time" (s 26(2)), which
--     "means 7 hours behind Coordinated Universal Time" (s 26(1)): so the beginning of a day is
--     07:00 UTC on that day, all year round, because the text fixes the offset and does not mention
--     daylight saving time.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `bc-interpretation-time`

GIVEN d  IS A DATE
      h  IS A NUMBER
      mi IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Pacific Time moment`
`test: Pacific Time moment` d h mi MEANS
    `Pacific Time moment` WITH `calendar day` IS d, `hour of the day` IS h, `minute of the hour` IS mi

GIVEN d  IS A DATE
      h  IS A NUMBER
      mi IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `UTC moment`
`test: UTC moment` d h mi MEANS
    `UTC moment` WITH `calendar day` IS d, `hour of the day` IS h, `minute of the hour` IS mi

§ `The Act says nothing about when it comes into force (assent 2026-03-10)`

-- The Lieutenant Governor assented on 2026-03-10.
#ASSERT `s 3(1) the date of assent to an Act` (`The Lieutenant Governor assented to the Act` (YMD 2026 3 10)) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 3 10)

-- No other date of commencement is provided: the date of assent (s 3(2)).
#ASSERT `s 3(2) the date of commencement of a portion of an Act` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 10)) `It provides no date of commencement` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 3 10)

-- It binds from the beginning of that day, in Pacific Time.
#ASSERT `the moment from which a portion of an Act binds` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 10)) `It provides no date of commencement` EQUALS JUST (`test: Pacific Time moment` (YMD 2026 3 10) 0 0)

-- That is 07:00 UTC on 2026-03-10.
#ASSERT `s 26 the UTC moment of a Pacific Time moment` (`s 4(1) the beginning of a day` (YMD 2026 3 10)) EQUALS `test: UTC moment` (YMD 2026 3 10) 7 0

-- The text speaks of the date of assent. It says nothing of "passed" or "published", so when only
-- one of those is known the caller has to supply the date of assent; nothing here guesses it.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 3 does not say that the day an Act was passed or published is its date of assent` (YMD 2026 3 10)
        BECAUSE "s 3 does not say that the day an Act was passed or published is its date of assent"

§ `The Act says it comes into force on a day to be fixed later (fixed as 2026-06-01)`

#ASSERT `s 3(2) the date of commencement of a portion of an Act` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 10)) (`It provides that it comes into force on proclamation or by regulation of the Lieutenant Governor in Council` (JUST (YMD 2026 6 1))) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 6 1)
#ASSERT `the moment from which a portion of an Act binds` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 10)) (`It provides that it comes into force on proclamation or by regulation of the Lieutenant Governor in Council` (JUST (YMD 2026 6 1))) EQUALS JUST (`test: Pacific Time moment` (YMD 2026 6 1) 0 0)
#ASSERT `s 26 the UTC moment of a Pacific Time moment` (`s 4(1) the beginning of a day` (YMD 2026 6 1)) EQUALS `test: UTC moment` (YMD 2026 6 1) 7 0

-- The provision that fixes the later day, and the title of the Act, are deemed in force on the
-- date of assent (s 3(3)).
#ASSERT `s 3(3) the day the commencement provision and the title of an Act are in force` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 10)) (`It provides that it comes into force on proclamation or by regulation of the Lieutenant Governor in Council` (JUST (YMD 2026 6 1))) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 3 10)

-- Until the day is fixed, the portion is not in force: no day and no moment.
#ASSERT `s 3(2) the date of commencement of a portion of an Act` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 10)) (`It provides that it comes into force on proclamation or by regulation of the Lieutenant Governor in Council` NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the moment from which a portion of an Act binds` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 10)) (`It provides that it comes into force on proclamation or by regulation of the Lieutenant Governor in Council` NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(3) the day the commencement provision and the title of an Act are in force` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 10)) (`It provides that it comes into force on proclamation or by regulation of the Lieutenant Governor in Council` NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 3 10)

§ `The Act names a day`

#ASSERT `s 3(2) the date of commencement of a portion of an Act` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 10)) (`It provides that it comes into force on a stated day` (YMD 2026 9 1)) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 9 1)
#ASSERT `the moment from which a portion of an Act binds` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 10)) (`It provides that it comes into force on a stated day` (YMD 2026 9 1)) EQUALS JUST (`test: Pacific Time moment` (YMD 2026 9 1) 0 0)

-- A day earlier than the date of assent: it comes into force on that day, retroactively (s 3(3.1)).
#ASSERT `s 3(2) the date of commencement of a portion of an Act` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 10)) (`It provides that it comes into force on a stated day` (YMD 2026 2 1)) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 2 1)
#ASSERT `s 3(3.1) a portion comes into force on a day earlier than the date of assent, and is retroactive` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 10)) (`It provides that it comes into force on a stated day` (YMD 2026 2 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 3(3.1) a portion comes into force on a day earlier than the date of assent, and is retroactive` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 10)) (`It provides that it comes into force on a stated day` (YMD 2026 3 10)))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 3(3.1) a portion comes into force on a day earlier than the date of assent, and is retroactive` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 10)) (`It provides that it comes into force on a stated day` (YMD 2026 9 1)))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 3(3.1) a portion comes into force on a day earlier than the date of assent, and is retroactive` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 10)) (`It provides that it comes into force on proclamation or by regulation of the Lieutenant Governor in Council` (JUST (YMD 2026 6 1))))
#ASSERT `s 3(3.1) a portion comes into force on a day earlier than the date of assent, and is retroactive` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 10)) (`It provides that it comes into force on proclamation or by regulation of the Lieutenant Governor in Council` (JUST (YMD 2026 2 15)))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 3(3.1) a portion comes into force on a day earlier than the date of assent, and is retroactive` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 10)) `It provides no date of commencement`)

§ `An Act reserved for the signification of the pleasure of the Governor General (s 3(1))`

-- The date of assent is the date of the signification, and the Act has no date of assent until then.
#ASSERT `s 3(1) the date of assent to an Act` (`The Act was reserved for the signification of the pleasure of the Governor General` (JUST (YMD 2026 4 20))) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 4 20)
#ASSERT `s 3(1) the date of assent to an Act` (`The Act was reserved for the signification of the pleasure of the Governor General` NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(2) the date of commencement of a portion of an Act` (`s 3(1) the date of assent to an Act` (`The Act was reserved for the signification of the pleasure of the Governor General` (JUST (YMD 2026 4 20)))) `It provides no date of commencement` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 4 20)
#ASSERT `s 3(2) the date of commencement of a portion of an Act` (`s 3(1) the date of assent to an Act` (`The Act was reserved for the signification of the pleasure of the Governor General` NOTHING)) `It provides no date of commencement` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `The moment: Pacific Time is 7 hours behind UTC all year (s 26)`

#ASSERT `s 26(1) the number of hours Pacific Time is behind UTC` EQUALS 7
-- A winter day: the text fixes the offset at 7 hours and says nothing of daylight saving time, so
-- the beginning of 2026-01-15 in Pacific Time is 07:00 UTC, as in summer.
#ASSERT `s 26 the UTC moment of a Pacific Time moment` (`s 4(1) the beginning of a day` (YMD 2026 1 15)) EQUALS `test: UTC moment` (YMD 2026 1 15) 7 0
-- A moment that is 17:00 in Pacific Time is 00:00 UTC on the next day; 16:59 is 23:59 on the same day.
#ASSERT `s 26 the UTC moment of a Pacific Time moment` (`test: Pacific Time moment` (YMD 2026 3 10) 17 0) EQUALS `test: UTC moment` (YMD 2026 3 11) 0 0
#ASSERT `s 26 the UTC moment of a Pacific Time moment` (`test: Pacific Time moment` (YMD 2026 3 10) 16 59) EQUALS `test: UTC moment` (YMD 2026 3 10) 23 59
#ASSERT `s 26 the UTC moment of a Pacific Time moment` (`test: Pacific Time moment` (YMD 2026 3 10) 23 30) EQUALS `test: UTC moment` (YMD 2026 3 11) 6 30
-- Across a month end and a year end.
#ASSERT `s 26 the UTC moment of a Pacific Time moment` (`test: Pacific Time moment` (YMD 2026 12 31) 20 0) EQUALS `test: UTC moment` (YMD 2027 1 1) 3 0

§ `Regulations (s 3(5))`

-- A regulation expressed to come into force on a particular day comes into force that day,
-- whatever its class.
#ASSERT `s 3(5) the day a regulation comes into force` (YMD 2026 3 10) `A regulation of any other class` (`It is expressed to come into force on a particular day` (YMD 2026 5 1)) EQUALS YMD 2026 5 1
#ASSERT `s 3(5) the day a regulation comes into force` (YMD 2026 3 10) `A regulation of a class exempted from the Regulations Act, or to which that Act does not apply` (`It is expressed to come into force on a particular day` (YMD 2026 5 1)) EQUALS YMD 2026 5 1

-- Worked case: made on 2026-03-10 and silent. Exempt (or outside the Regulations Act): the day it
-- was enacted, from the beginning of that day (s 4(1): "enactment" includes a regulation, s 1).
#ASSERT `s 3(5) the day a regulation comes into force` (YMD 2026 3 10) `A regulation of a class exempted from the Regulations Act, or to which that Act does not apply` `It is not expressed to come into force on a particular day` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 10
#ASSERT `the moment from which a regulation binds` (YMD 2026 3 10) `A regulation of a class exempted from the Regulations Act, or to which that Act does not apply` `It is not expressed to come into force on a particular day` EQUALS `test: Pacific Time moment` (YMD 2026 3 10) 0 0
#ASSERT `the moment from which a regulation binds` (YMD 2026 3 10) `A regulation of any other class` (`It is expressed to come into force on a particular day` (YMD 2026 5 1)) EQUALS `test: Pacific Time moment` (YMD 2026 5 1) 0 0

-- Any other regulation that names no day: s 3(5) does not say, and s 3(2) speaks of an Act and of
-- assent. The Regulations Act governs and is not in this text.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 3(5) the day a regulation comes into force` (YMD 2026 3 10) `A regulation of any other class` `It is not expressed to come into force on a particular day`
        BECAUSE "s 3(5) does not say when a regulation of any other class that names no day comes into force"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the moment from which a regulation binds` (YMD 2026 3 10) `A regulation of any other class` `It is not expressed to come into force on a particular day`

§ `s 16(2) A proclamation dated the day its issue was authorized`

#ASSERT `s 16(2) the day a proclamation takes effect` (YMD 2026 5 1) (YMD 2026 5 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 5 1
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 16(2) the day a proclamation takes effect` (YMD 2026 5 2) (YMD 2026 5 1)
        BECAUSE "s 16(2) does not say when a proclamation takes effect if it is not dated the day its issue was authorized"

§ `s 4(2) and (3) When an enactment ceases to have effect`

-- Repealed and replaced: it ceases at the time the new enactment commences, the beginning of that day.
#ASSERT `s 4(2) the moment an enactment that is repealed and replaced ceases to have effect` (YMD 2026 9 1) EQUALS `test: Pacific Time moment` (YMD 2026 9 1) 0 0
-- Any other: at the end of the day on which it expires, which is the beginning of the next day.
#ASSERT `s 4(3) the moment any other enactment ceases to have effect` (YMD 2026 12 31) EQUALS `test: Pacific Time moment` (YMD 2027 1 1) 0 0
#ASSERT `s 4(3) the end of a day` (YMD 2026 3 10) EQUALS `test: Pacific Time moment` (YMD 2026 3 11) 0 0

§ `s 29 "commencement" and "now"`

#ASSERT `s 29 the commencement of an enactment` (YMD 2026 3 10) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 10
#ASSERT `s 29 the time that the word now refers to` (YMD 2026 3 10) EQUALS `test: Pacific Time moment` (YMD 2026 3 10) 0 0
